{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"artifacthub/community-operators/api-operator","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:17:00.612Z","source":{"name":"Artifact Hub","api":"https://artifacthub.io/api/v1/packages/olm/community-operators/api-operator","page":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/olm/community-operators/api-operator"},"readme":"## API Operator for deploying Integrations\n\nThe API operator for Kubernetes provides first-class support for Micro Integrator deployments in the Kubernetes\necosystem. It uses the Integration custom resource (integration_cr.yaml file) that is available in the Kubernetes\nproject (exported from WSO2 Integration Studio) and deploys the integration in your Kubernetes environment.\n\n![Alt text](images/K8s-API-Operator.png?raw=true \"K8s API Operator\")\n\n## Use the following command to install default configs for API Operator\n\n```sh\n>> kubectl apply -f https://github.com/wso2/k8s-api-operator/releases/download/v2.0.0/api-operator-operatorhub-configs.yaml\n```\n\n## Deploying Integrations\n\nDeploy integrations using K8s API Operator, see [Deploying Integrations using the Operator](https://apim.docs.wso2.com/en/4.0.0/install-and-setup/setup/kubernetes-operators/k8s-api-operator/manage-integrations/integration-deployments/).\n\n## Documentation\n\nYou can find the documentation [here](https://apim.docs.wso2.com/en/4.0.0/reference/k8s-operators/k8s-api-operator/).","readmeBase":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators","publisher":{"name":"Operator Framework","url":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/search?org=operator-framework","official":false,"verified":false,"cncf":false},"registered":null,"updated":"2021-04-28T10:00:00.000Z","categories":["Integration and delivery"],"keywords":["API","ManagedAPI","APIManagement","Cloud-native","Security","Ratelimiting","Analytics","Developer Tools","Integration & Delivery","Cloud Provider"],"license":null,"links":[{"name":"Documentation","url":"https://apim.docs.wso2.com/en/